Build the novadeck module.

grub-core/Makefile.core.def is GRUB's module manifest. Adding a stanza here is
the whole change; everything else is generated. boot/grub.sh runs ./autogen.sh
after applying this patch, which regenerates grub-core/Makefile.core.am (via
gentpl.py + autogen) and then the Makefile.in files (via autoreconf).

Regenerating rather than patching the generated files is deliberate. The .am
hunk autogen produces is mechanical and could be carried in a patch, but the
Makefile.in it feeds is not: re-running automake at all rewrites 23 files in the
tree and 191 hunks of grub-core/Makefile.in alone, because Ubuntu's automake is
not the automake the 2.14 tarball was released with. There is no version of that
diff worth keeping in a patch file.

`enable = efi` builds the module for every EFI target; only arm64-efi is ever
used here. Unlike Valve's steamenv stanza this needs no
-Wno-error=address-of-packed-member: novadeck.c reads and assigns packed struct
members but never takes their address.

diff -urN a/grub-core/Makefile.core.def b/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
--- a/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
+++ b/grub-core/Makefile.core.def
@@ -843,6 +843,12 @@
 };
 
 module = {
+  name = novadeck;
+  common = commands/efi/novadeck.c;
+  enable = efi;
+};
+
+module = {
   name = efitextmode;
   efi = commands/efi/efitextmode.c;
   enable = efi;
